  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level from all outcomes and comparing which lottery has a higher chance of exceeding it. The relevant information (aspiration level = ~1668.33, positive differences only possible in Lottery A) is not reflected in the verbal report. The individual instead focuses on the low probability of success in Lottery A and the certainty in Lottery B, which aligns more with a certainty effect or risk aversion, not aspiration-level reasoning. The justification in the report is probabilistic and outcome-avoidant (avoiding near-certain loss), whereas the reason is based on outcome comparisons relative to a computed mean. There is no overlap in the information considered or the decision rule applied. Therefore, it is certain that the aspiration-level reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
